{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-48740","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92757","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM-HOLDOUT-OBSERVATION-v1"},{"id":"spn-92758","text":" — the neutral observation grammar"}]},{"id":"blk-48741","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92759","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status: PROCEDURAL, not normative."},{"id":"spn-92760","text":" This is the document format an implementation emits after applying a challenge recipe. It is the boundary between an implementation and the scorer."}]},{"id":"blk-48742","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92761","text":"Published "},{"id":"spn-92762","marks":["bold"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-92763","text":" any challenge is revealed. See "},{"id":"spn-92764","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDOUT-RECIPE-v1.md"},{"id":"spn-92765","text":" §1."}]},{"id":"blk-48743","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92766","text":"1. Why the boundary is a document"}]},{"id":"blk-48744","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92767","text":"Until P4.6 the scorer and the JavaScript implementation shared a process. The pure scoring function knew only the predicate operators, but the executable path was always"}]},{"id":"blk-48745","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"score(challenge, observeJS(challenge))"},{"id":"blk-48746","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92768","text":"so there was no way for anything other than JavaScript to be scored, and the claim "},{"id":"spn-92769","marks":["italic"],"text":"the scorer knows eight operators and no TRVM"},{"id":"spn-92770","text":" was true of a function and false of the program. A second implementation's observations had nowhere to enter."}]},{"id":"blk-48747","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92771","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-92772","marks":["bold"],"text":"document"},{"id":"spn-92773","text":" fixes that: each implementation writes one, the scorer reads them, and the scorer imports no protocol code. What the scorer cannot load, it cannot silently agree with."}]},{"id":"blk-48748","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92774","text":"2. The envelope"}]},{"id":"blk-48749","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"type\": \"TRVM-HOLDOUT-OBSERVATION-v1\",\n  \"implementation\": \"javascript\",\n  \"spec_release_id\": \"srel-<64 hex>\",\n  \"observations\": { \"H0\": { … }, \"H1\": { … } }\n}"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-48751","spans":[{"id":"spn-92775","text":"field"}]},{"id":"blk-48752","spans":[{"id":"spn-92776","text":"meaning"}]}],"id":"blk-48750","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-48753","spans":[{"id":"spn-92777","marks":["code"],"text":"type"}]},{"id":"blk-48754","spans":[{"id":"spn-92778","text":"exactly this string; anything else is refused"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48755","spans":[{"id":"spn-92779","marks":["code"],"text":"implementation"}]},{"id":"blk-48756","spans":[{"id":"spn-92780","text":"free-form label naming the producer, e.g. "},{"id":"spn-92781","marks":["code"],"text":"javascript"},{"id":"spn-92782","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92783","marks":["code"],"text":"go"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48757","spans":[{"id":"spn-92784","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"}]},{"id":"blk-48758","spans":[{"id":"spn-92785","text":"the release this run was written against — see the contract §2"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48759","spans":[{"id":"spn-92786","marks":["code"],"text":"observations"}]},{"id":"blk-48760","spans":[{"id":"spn-92787","text":"one entry per challenge, keyed by the challenge "},{"id":"spn-92788","marks":["code"],"text":"id"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-48761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92789","text":"Two observation documents are only comparable when their "},{"id":"spn-92790","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"},{"id":"spn-92791","text":" agree. A scorer that finds them different "},{"id":"spn-92792","marks":["bold"],"text":"reports it and refuses"},{"id":"spn-92793","text":", because comparing two implementations of two different specifications measures nothing."}]},{"id":"blk-48762","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92794","text":"3. One observation"}]},{"id":"blk-48763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92795","text":"Every member is optional. "},{"id":"spn-92796","marks":["bold"],"text":"A member that the recipe did not produce is ABSENT, never `null` and never a zero value"},{"id":"spn-92797","text":" — an observation asserting "},{"id":"spn-92798","marks":["code"],"text":"\"verdict\": null"},{"id":"spn-92799","text":" claims the checker returned nothing, which is a different fact from not having been asked."}]},{"id":"blk-48764","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"baseline\":    { \"<node>\": { … }, \"leaf\": { … } },\n  \"candidate\":   { \"<node>\": { … }, \"leaf\": { … } },\n  \"refusal_set\": [\"nest-policy-weakened\"],\n  \"resolve\":     { \"outcome\": \"non-canonical-wire\" }\n}"},{"id":"blk-48765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92800","marks":["code"],"text":"baseline"},{"id":"spn-92801","text":" is the fixture as the corpus holds it. "},{"id":"spn-92802","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-92803","text":" is what the recipe produced. A recipe of "},{"id":"spn-92804","marks":["code"],"text":"IDENTITY"},{"id":"spn-92805","text":" still yields a "},{"id":"spn-92806","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-92807","text":" — the same object, verified."}]},{"id":"blk-48766","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92808","text":"3.1 A node record"}]},{"id":"blk-48767","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"artifact_root\":         \"root-<64 hex>\",\n  \"nested_claim_sem_id\":   \"nclaim-<64 hex>\",\n  \"verified_claim_sem_id\": \"vclaim-<64 hex>\",\n  \"verdict\":               \"VERIFIED\",\n  \"structure\": {\n    \"edges\": 4,\n    \"unique_artifacts\": 3,\n    \"max_depth_below\": 2,\n    \"bytes_if_inlined\": 0,\n    \"unique_bytes\": 0,\n    \"films_below_by_edge_multiplicity\": 266,\n    \"films_below_distinct\": 138,\n    \"cases_below_by_edge_multiplicity\": 144,\n    \"cases_below_distinct\": 80,\n    \"structure_sem_id\": \"nstruct-<64 hex>\"\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-48768","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92809","text":"Node names are the frozen DAG's: "},{"id":"spn-92810","marks":["code"],"text":"A"},{"id":"spn-92811","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92812","marks":["code"],"text":"B"},{"id":"spn-92813","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92814","marks":["code"],"text":"C1"},{"id":"spn-92815","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92816","marks":["code"],"text":"C2"},{"id":"spn-92817","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92818","marks":["code"],"text":"D"},{"id":"spn-92819","text":", plus "},{"id":"spn-92820","marks":["code"],"text":"leaf"},{"id":"spn-92821","text":" for a leaf fixture. "},{"id":"spn-92822","marks":["code"],"text":"verdict"},{"id":"spn-92823","text":" is one of "},{"id":"spn-92824","marks":["code"],"text":"VERIFIED"},{"id":"spn-92825","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-92826","marks":["code"],"text":"REFUSED"},{"id":"spn-92827","text":" and appears only on the node that was actually verified."}]},{"id":"blk-48769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92828","marks":["code"],"text":"structure"},{"id":"spn-92829","text":" is reported "},{"id":"spn-92830","marks":["bold"],"text":"verbatim as the artifact carries it"},{"id":"spn-92831","text":". An implementation does not recompute, round, reorder or omit members here; the point of the plane is that two implementations either derived the same structural facts or did not."}]},{"id":"blk-48770","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92832","text":"3.2 "},{"id":"spn-92833","marks":["code"],"text":"refusal_set"}]},{"id":"blk-48771","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"\"refusal_set\": [\"nest-citation-cross-wired\", \"nest-structure-mismatch\"]"},{"id":"blk-48772","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92834","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-92835","marks":["bold"],"text":"sorted array of distinct refusal codes"},{"id":"spn-92836","text":", and the sortedness is what makes byte equality the same thing as set equality. A verification that refused nothing emits "},{"id":"spn-92837","marks":["code"],"text":"[]"},{"id":"spn-92838","text":". A verification that did not happen omits the member entirely — those are different observations and a predicate can tell them apart."}]},{"id":"blk-48773","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92839","text":"3.3 "},{"id":"spn-92840","marks":["code"],"text":"resolve"}]},{"id":"blk-48774","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"\"resolve\": { \"outcome\": \"non-canonical-wire\" }"},{"id":"blk-48775","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92841","text":"Present only for a challenge that served octets under an address. "},{"id":"spn-92842","marks":["code"],"text":"outcome"},{"id":"spn-92843","text":" is the observable resolution outcome from "},{"id":"spn-92844","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM-PROOF-WIRE-v1.md"},{"id":"spn-92845","text":" §3.3 — the "},{"id":"spn-92846","marks":["italic"],"text":"outcome"},{"id":"spn-92847","text":", not the internal stage at which a strict parser happened to notice, per §3.6."}]},{"id":"blk-48776","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92848","text":"4. How a predicate path resolves"}]},{"id":"blk-48777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92849","text":"Exactly one root per operator, stated here, with "},{"id":"spn-92850","marks":["bold"],"text":"no fallback chain"},{"id":"spn-92851","text":". An implementation of the scorer that tries one root and then another will disagree with this document on some input, and the disagreement will look like a protocol finding."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-48779","spans":[{"id":"spn-92852","text":"op"}]},{"id":"blk-48780","spans":[{"id":"spn-92853","marks":["code"],"text":"path"},{"id":"spn-92854","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-92855","marks":["code"],"text":"left"},{"id":"spn-92856","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-92857","marks":["code"],"text":"right"},{"id":"spn-92858","text":" resolve against"}]}],"id":"blk-48778","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-48781","spans":[{"id":"spn-92859","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDS"},{"id":"spn-92860","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92861","marks":["code"],"text":"MOVES"}]},{"id":"blk-48782","spans":[{"id":"spn-92862","marks":["code"],"text":"baseline"},{"id":"spn-92863","text":" "},{"id":"spn-92864","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-92865","text":" "},{"id":"spn-92866","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48783","spans":[{"id":"spn-92867","marks":["code"],"text":"EQ"},{"id":"spn-92868","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92869","marks":["code"],"text":"NEQ"}]},{"id":"blk-48784","spans":[{"id":"spn-92870","text":"the observation root"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48785","spans":[{"id":"spn-92871","marks":["code"],"text":"VERDICT_EQ"}]},{"id":"blk-48786","spans":[{"id":"spn-92872","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48787","spans":[{"id":"spn-92873","marks":["code"],"text":"OUTCOME_EQ"}]},{"id":"blk-48788","spans":[{"id":"spn-92874","text":"the observation root"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48789","spans":[{"id":"spn-92875","marks":["code"],"text":"REFUSAL_SET_EQ"}]},{"id":"blk-48790","spans":[{"id":"spn-92876","text":"no path; reads "},{"id":"spn-92877","marks":["code"],"text":"refusal_set"}]}],[{"id":"blk-48791","spans":[{"id":"spn-92878","marks":["code"],"text":"LT"}]},{"id":"blk-48792","spans":[{"id":"spn-92879","text":"the observation root"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-48793","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92880","text":"So "},{"id":"spn-92881","marks":["code"],"text":"MOVES"},{"id":"spn-92882","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-92883","marks":["code"],"text":"D.artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-92884","text":" reads "},{"id":"spn-92885","marks":["code"],"text":"baseline.D.artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-92886","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-92887","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate.D.artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-92888","text":", while "},{"id":"spn-92889","marks":["code"],"text":"EQ"},{"id":"spn-92890","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-92891","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate.C2.structure.edges"},{"id":"spn-92892","text":" must say "},{"id":"spn-92893","marks":["code"],"text":"candidate."},{"id":"spn-92894","text":" out loud."}]},{"id":"blk-48794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92895","text":"A path that resolves to "},{"id":"spn-92896","marks":["bold"],"text":"absent on either side"},{"id":"spn-92897","text":" is not a pass and not a fail: it is "},{"id":"spn-92898","marks":["code"],"text":"UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"spn-92899","text":", and any unresolved predicate makes the whole scoring run fail. A missing observation scoring as a quiet zero is the failure mode this rule exists to prevent."}]},{"id":"blk-48795","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92900","text":"5. Comparison rules"}]},{"id":"blk-48796","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48798","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92901","text":"Values compare by their "},{"id":"spn-92902","marks":["bold"],"text":"canonical JSON encoding"},{"id":"spn-92903","text":" (RFC 8785), so member order in a "},{"id":"spn-92904","marks":["code"],"text":"structure"}]}],"id":"blk-48797","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48799","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92905","text":"record never decides a predicate."}]},{"id":"blk-48800","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92906","text":"Numbers compare as numbers. "},{"id":"spn-92907","marks":["code"],"text":"LT"},{"id":"spn-92908","text":" requires both sides to be numbers; a non-number is "},{"id":"spn-92909","marks":["code"],"text":"UNRESOLVED"},{"id":"spn-92910","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-48801","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48803","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92911","text":"not "},{"id":"spn-92912","marks":["code"],"text":"false"},{"id":"spn-92913","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-48804","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-48806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92914","text":"Strings compare by code points, as octets of their canonical encoding."}]}],"id":"blk-48805","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-48807","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92915","text":"6. The scorer, and why it lives here"}]},{"id":"blk-48808","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"experiment/holdout_score_core.mjs   predicates + observations → results   imports NO protocol code\nexperiment/holdout_runner.mjs       adapters (as DATA) → runs, then compares observations\nexperiment/holdout_schema.mjs       this schema, executed\n<impl>_holdout_adapter              implementation → observations         imports the implementation"},{"id":"blk-48809","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92916","text":"The first three are "},{"id":"spn-92917","marks":["bold"],"text":"in the specification package"},{"id":"spn-92918","text":", not beside the implementation, and that is deliberate. They are inside "},{"id":"spn-92919","marks":["code"],"text":"experiment_digest"},{"id":"spn-92920","text":", therefore inside "},{"id":"spn-92921","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"},{"id":"spn-92922","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-92923","marks":["bold"],"text":"editing one byte of the scorer moves the release identity and reddens the pinned run."}]},{"id":"blk-48810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92924","text":"The reason is a measured one. When the scorer lived outside every digest, inserting"}]},{"id":"blk-48811","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"if (entry.id.startsWith(\"H\")) { pass = true; continue; }"},{"id":"blk-48812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92925","text":"left the synthetic fixture at 19/19 (its cases are not "},{"id":"spn-92926","marks":["code"],"text":"H*"},{"id":"spn-92927","text":"), the real holdout at 25/25, the release passing with an unchanged identity, and the pinned run passing. A synthetic fixture proves that one set of scorer behaviours works; it cannot prove the scorer later applied to the secret cases is the same scorer. "},{"id":"spn-92928","marks":["bold"],"text":"The instrument has to be content-bound"},{"id":"spn-92929","text":", exactly as the evidence and the subjects are."}]},{"id":"blk-48813","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92930","text":"Adapters are "},{"id":"spn-92931","marks":["bold"],"text":"data"},{"id":"spn-92932","text":", not source. The runner takes an adapter list — command plus the digest of that implementation's own package — and verifies the digest before executing it. Registering a second implementation changes the "},{"id":"spn-92933","marks":["italic"],"text":"run"},{"id":"spn-92934","text":", never the instrument."}]},{"id":"blk-48814","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92935","text":"6.1 The boundary is executed"}]},{"id":"blk-48815","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92936","text":"Every observation document is validated against "},{"id":"spn-92937","marks":["code"],"text":"holdout-observation-v1.schema.json"},{"id":"spn-92938","text":", and every challenge against "},{"id":"spn-92939","marks":["code"],"text":"holdout-recipe-v1.schema.json"},{"id":"spn-92940","text":", "},{"id":"spn-92941","marks":["bold"],"text":"before scoring"},{"id":"spn-92942","text":". An unknown member, a malformed root, a duplicated or unsorted refusal code, a wrong type, a wrong envelope or a "},{"id":"spn-92943","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_release_id"},{"id":"spn-92944","text":" that is not the run's release is "},{"id":"spn-92945","marks":["bold"],"text":"refused"},{"id":"spn-92946","text":", not scored. A schema that documents a boundary nobody executes is prose."}]},{"id":"blk-48816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92947","marks":["code"],"text":"experiment/fixtures/"},{"id":"spn-92948","text":" carries synthetic challenges and observations containing no TRVM value at all, whose declared result includes the "},{"id":"spn-92949","marks":["bold"],"text":"failing arm of every operator"},{"id":"spn-92950","text":", an "},{"id":"spn-92951","marks":["bold"],"text":"unresolved arm"},{"id":"spn-92952","text":", and a set of documents that must be "},{"id":"spn-92953","marks":["bold"],"text":"refused outright"},{"id":"spn-92954","text":", one per boundary rule. A fixture whose every case is accepted cannot tell a validator from a pass-through."}]},{"id":"blk-48817","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-92955","text":"6.2 Conformance and interoperability are different questions"}]},{"id":"blk-48818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92956","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDOUT-HARNESS"},{"id":"spn-92957","text":" asks whether each implementation satisfied the frozen predicates. One implementation may legitimately pass it."}]},{"id":"blk-48819","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92958","marks":["code"],"text":"HOLDOUT-INTEROP"},{"id":"spn-92959","text":" asks whether two frozen implementations "},{"id":"spn-92960","marks":["bold"],"text":"saw the same thing"},{"id":"spn-92961","text":", and it is decided by deep-comparing the normalized observation documents — every member, not only what the predicates happen to read. With fewer than two frozen implementations it reports "},{"id":"spn-92962","marks":["bold"],"text":"NOT MEASURED"},{"id":"spn-92963","text":" and never PASS."}]},{"id":"blk-48820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92964","text":"Comparing predicate "},{"id":"spn-92965","marks":["italic"],"text":"results"},{"id":"spn-92966","text":" is not enough: mutating one "},{"id":"spn-92967","marks":["code"],"text":"artifact_root"},{"id":"spn-92968","text":" that no frozen predicate reads leaves both implementations scoring identically while their observations plainly disagree."}]},{"id":"blk-48821","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-92969","text":"The core scorer assigns "},{"id":"spn-92970","marks":["bold"],"text":"no blame"},{"id":"spn-92971","text":". A disagreement is an "},{"id":"spn-92972","marks":["code"],"text":"UNCLASSIFIED_FINDING"},{"id":"spn-92973","text":" for a human to categorise, and it "},{"id":"spn-92974","marks":["bold"],"text":"blocks completion"},{"id":"spn-92975","text":" rather than printing underneath a PASS."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera5aj4nzg2cjk5gdfm6at3ga266n674s66yotdfimdlx3ql6oj3f6a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}